{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiSwcx8ccLsqLVwtnT1A","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LymYnNW1BhSuUG5tGofgos","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"$WSROOT/laya/s1/opus-r2/step3/NOTES.md","content":"# Step 3 notes\n\n**Change.** I left every existing weight as it was and added one new AND-gate group to the extra module (8 step units, then 1 AND unit, with output weight +0.6). The group fires only on the account_security option vector, and only when:\n\n- **Option gate.** Conditions W0 columns 40/44/46, copied from the existing disabled third group (its output weight is 0), with their thresholds raised by 2. They pass on the AS option for 77–92% of my messages and on the other options for ≤5%.\n- **No AS spike.** The projection on the mean (AS − transfers) offset of my identity messages must stay under 14M. Real PIN and identity messages spike above 16M. This keeps PIN routed as before (correction 2).\n\n**Why so small.** Eligibility messages trigger no option's \"match spike\". The AS and transfers vectors are nearly identical for them, and every content direction I derived from my own messages separated eligibility from other messages at only ~0.6–0.75 AUC. So the boost acts mostly on low-margin messages, and +0.6 is the point where harm starts to rise steeply.\n\n**Measured on my messages.** Eligibility routed to AS: 45%, up from 3%. Other routes changed: 2.8%. PIN and FX unchanged. Evidence: 23/32 correct, up from 16/32.\n\n**Known gap.** scorer_in already fails correction 2 on 10 of my 13 PIN phrasings. I did not fix that.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2082,"cache_read_input_tokens":205220,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2082},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed