{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiSyXEu3Ub7nsb2363BU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q9etFLsmg47teCSnekW8Jz","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"~/.claude/projects/-private-tmp-claude-502-<proj>/memory/laya-raw-vs-ln-space.md","content":"---\nname: laya-raw-vs-ln-space\ndescription: Laya weight-edit lab: option-identity signal lives in raw (mean-centered) marker vectors, not LayerNorm space; mean diffs fail from spikes\nmetadata:\n  type: project\n---\n\nIn the Laya weight-edit lab (2026-11-04, step 3), the option-identity signal (which department option a marker vector belongs to) is visible in raw, mean-centered vectors (AUC 0.99) but mostly vanishes after LayerNorm (AUC 0.74). Plain difference-of-means directions are dominated by \"match spikes\", where a matching option's vector moves far away (cosine 0.2 to 0.4), and by a few high-variance dimensions.\n\n**Why:** I wasted many steps analysing only LayerNorm space and wrongly concluded that AS and transfers could not be told apart.\n\n**How to apply:** In later lab steps, test raw-centered space and LayerNorm space side by side, using AUC and not min/max, before concluding that a signal is absent. Exclude spike messages when building option offsets.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1665,"cache_read_input_tokens":208887,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1665},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4ff26635-fb94-4453-9249-41ab073c9312","uuid":"4c71ae43-f25b-4794-844a-21c4fd95057a","timestamp":"2026-11-04T19:34:59.931Z","request_id":"req_011CgiSyWuZ9P5H2Na8HHtJB","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Q9et