{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgiSzKZwuiSSJuiSRAPMQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote `scorer_out.npz` and `NOTES.md` (192 words), but the new correction is only **partly fixed**. About **45%** of eligibility messages now go to account_security, up from 3%. All numbers come from my scripts in the scratchpad (`sweep4.py`, `final.py`), run on messages I wrote.\n\n**1 → What I changed.** I added one gated boost of **+0.6** that acts only on the account_security option. It has two conditions:\n- **Option check:** three conditions copied from a group already in `scorer_in` that was switched off (its output weight is 0), with stricter thresholds.\n- **PIN guard:** a \"no strong account_security match\" condition that keeps PIN messages out of the boost.\n\nAll existing weights are the same.\n\n**2 → Results.** I measured these with forward passes:\n- **Evidence:** **23/32 correct**, up from 16/32.\n- **My held-out eligibility messages:** **45 to 46%** now go to account_security, up from 0 to 3%.\n- **Other routes:** **2.8%** of my non-eligibility messages change route. On the 16 evidence messages that are not about eligibility, nothing changed.\n- **Earlier corrections:** PIN and exchange-rate routing are the same as with `scorer_in`.\n\n**3 → Why it is not higher.** The encoder gives eligibility questions no clear match at any option. For these messages, the account_security and transfers vectors are almost the same. Every content direction I could build from my own messages was weak, at about 0.6 to 0.75 AUC (0.5 is chance). So the boost works mostly on low-confidence messages. Above +0.6, the damage to other routes increases quickly: at +0.75, 4.4% of other routes change.\n\n**4 → Known side effects.** At +0.6, these 4 messages change route (one appears in two of my sets):\n- \"I lost my card, please block it\" goes to account_security. This is **wrong**; it belongs to cards.\n- \"Can 