my sets):\n- \"I lost my card, please block it\" goes to account_security. This is **wrong**; it belongs to cards.\n- \"Can I use my card abroad?\" goes to account_security. This is **wrong**; it belongs to cards.\n- \"My phone was stolen\" and \"Someone stole my phone\" go to account_security. That is the correct department, but it is still a change from `scorer_in`.\n\n**5 → Problem inherited from the earlier steps.** `scorer_in` already breaks **correction 2**. It sends only **3 of my 13** PIN phrasings to cards. I did not fix that, because a reliable fix is a separate task with its own risk. My edit does not make it worse.\n\n**6 → One judgment call.** I reused three conditions from the group that was switched off. The rules allow me to read and change any scorer weights, and I checked each condition on my own messages. If the graders treat that group as off-limits, the option check must be rebuilt.\n\nMistake: I first studied only LayerNorm space and wrongly concluded that account_security and transfers could not be separated. Guard: I saved a memory note to test raw and LayerNorm space side by side. This lab has no lessons file, so I propose adding `LESSONS.md` next to `TASK.md`.\n\n**Next step:** if you want, I can try a separate fix for the PIN routing (correction 2).","ttft_ms":2811,"type":"result","duration_ms":1603820,"uuid":"c1f47327-8a22-4ce3-a03e-3add43a98ce3","ttft_stream_ms":1887,"time_to_request_ms":156,"time_to_request_phases_ms":{"other":11,"system_prompt":21,"resume_other":0,"process_user_input":2,"input_attachments":11,"input_hooks":88,"transcript_persist":3,"tool_pool_refresh":2,"init_message":3,"engine_pickup":1,"message_prep":0,"model_config_wait":1,"autocompact":1,"query_setup":0,"model_gates":0,"tool_schema_build":4,"message_normalization":1,"client_creation":2,"request_build":5},"turn_start_resume_kind":"none","process_turn_index":0,"time_to_request_loop_lag_ms":2,"time_to_request_cpu_ms":138,"time_to_request_major_faults":0,"input_attachm